@flexiarg snatch/consult-the-remedy-before-exiting
@title Consult the Remedy Before Exiting
@audience players, policy authors
@tone practical
@style pattern
@why snatch/revert-then-invert snatch/mark-without-force

! conclusion: Before abstaining after a defection, check what the arrangement entitles you to and use it.

  + context: **Play grain.** Written 2026-08-27 from a playout finding: under G4
    the remedies `mark-without-force` and `revert-then-invert` became applicable
    from round 2 onward, and a grim-trigger policy had already left the game, so
    they were **applicable and unused in every remaining round**.

  + IF:
    You have been defected against, and the arrangement provides a mark, an
    adjudicator, or any other response.

  + HOWEVER:
    A policy written for the state of nature exits on the first defection, and
    exiting is indistinguishable — from the outside and from the policy itself —
    whether or not a remedy existed.

  + THEN:
    Consult the remedies the arrangement provides before exiting, and record that
    you did so, including when you decline them.

  + BECAUSE:
    Exiting forfeits an entitlement you were granted, and a policy that never
    consults the institution it plays inside is playing a different, poorer game.
    Availability is not use.
    + evidence: `futon3/checks/playout_snatch.clj`, G4 rounds 2–5.
